@startuml
!include ../../../../../../tooling/styles/plantuml/structural/component-diagram-style.iuml

title The Allowed-to-Use Relation\nPermissions define valid dependencies; violations break the architecture

rectangle "Layer C\n**Presentation**" as C $fill_primary
rectangle "Layer B\n**Business Logic**" as B $fill_ok
rectangle "Layer A\n**Data Access**" as A $fill_caution

C -[$line_ok]-> B : allowed
B -[$line_ok]-> A : allowed

C -[$line_caution,dashed]-> A : allowed\n//(relaxed only)//

A -[$line_invalid]-> C : **VIOLATION**\n//upward dependency//

legend right
  | Arrow | Meaning |
  |<$deep_ok> | Allowed dependency |
  |<$line_caution> ~~~ | Relaxed-only permission |
  |<$deep_invalid> | Architectural violation |
end legend

note bottom
  **Key properties:**
  * Defines permissions, not requirements
  * Transitivity depends on strict vs. relaxed rules
  * Violations indicate architectural erosion
end note
@enduml
